 virtual reality simulator</article-title><source>J Am Coll Surg</source><year>2002</year><volume>195</volume><fpage>675</fpage><lpage>681</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12437255</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-wjem-9-0141"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crutcher</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Where Canadian family physicians learn procedural skills</article-title><source>Fam Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>491</fpage><lpage>495</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15988634</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-wjem-9-0141"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van der Vlugt</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Harter</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Teaching procedural skills to medical students: one institution&#x02019;s experience with an emergency procedures course</article-title><source>Ann Emerg Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>41</fpage><lpage>49</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12085072</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-wjem-9-0141"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Training fourth-year medical students in critical invasive skills improves subsequent patient safety</article-title><source>Am Surg</source><year>2003</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>437</fpage><lpage>440</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12769219</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16-wjem-9-0141"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tabas</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><etal/></person-